// Type-checks the TESTS, which no tsconfig covered before.
//
// `tsconfig.json` has `"include": ["src"]`, so `tsc --noEmit` never looked at tests at
// all — a type error in a test surfaced only when jest happened to run that file. That
// is how a fourth `new UserService(...)` call site survived a green typecheck.
//
// Strict here is what makes a test DOUBLE honest: a fake typed against the real
// interface fails to compile when it drifts, instead of silently standing in for a
// method it does not have. Two fakes missing `.where()` inside transactions is exactly
// the bug this closes.
//
// CommonJS + jest types mirror what ts-jest actually compiles with (jest.config.cjs).
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "module": "CommonJS",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "types": ["node", "express", "jest"]
  },
  "include": ["src", "tests"]
}
